[Music]  every single day i look at what is being  wasted and i find a way to actually put  it back in the circle we call this  circular economy so the idea is to  create value out of waste  my name is david cote i'm co-founder of  luke mission  so loot mission started five years ago  we basically rescue food every day and  make different products out of it so we  rescue  produce and we make cold pressed juice  out of them and then when our own pulp  and fiber is reused after to actually  make your dog treats we've launched a  line of beer made out of the old bread  we have a gin made out of potato  cuttings we have soap made with  discarded oil from a fast food chain we  look at waste and we try to find  solution to put it back in on the on the  shelves in the grocery store and create  value out of it  so what's amazing with our products is  that we have a flavor profile that is  different in our competition in the  industry when you make a product we have  to look at costing all the time and make  sure your casting is as low as possible  so if i take cold press juices for  example most of our computer on the  market use the same thing cucumber  celery  carrot and beets things that are not too  pricey we work with overstock so we have  access to clementine fresh grapes fennel  honeydew melon things that normally you  wouldn't see in a culprit juice because  most of companies can't afford it  [Music]  food waste  is a huge cause of greenhouse gas  emissions because when you send food to  the landfill even though instinctively  you think it's the most natural thing  you can send to the landfill it's  actually the worst thing we can send  because it doesn't decompose because we  fill the lamb so it creates a lake civic  which is a basically an acidic  liquid that contaminates biodiversity so  by stopping food waste we're stopping a  huge cause of greenhouse gas emission  and kind of giving us a little chance  for the future  i always felt like i wanted to do  something for the planet i realized that  the best thing you can do is start a  business that actually change the world  and change the environment because  that's where money is at and money  change the world you have to talk to  their pockets  [Music]  [Applause]  i'll say we pay about  35 to 40 the price that the normal  company will pay for normal produce high  price but we think that's the best  reward we can give to companies that  wants to look at their food waste and  wants to try to find a solution with us  not too long ago sobey that i wanted  carrots that they wanted to give us and  i said no we'll buy this van from you  because this is what we want to teach  people there's value in this waste  the difference with a linear company and  a circular economy company is that we're  not really looking for a gap in the  market we're looking at a problem and we  need to find a solution so every product  we launch we always have to look at what  is being wasted to create this product  take the gin for example someone called  me and said they're throwing away potato  cuttings so we went and visit looked at  what it looked like and then started  calling a few people in r d to see what  we could do with potato cuttings realize  we could make a gin so we sent it to a  distillery then we tested with buyers in  the market to see if there was an  interest  every single product is like this  and we want to replicate this model all  around the world right it doesn't make  sense to export our products to europe  or australia or even mexico or even  california because there's so much  transportation in need and and the waste  is everywhere so our idea is to actually  replicate this model and create a  factory just like we have here  all around the world  i feel every single day that i wake up  and i go to bed that i did something  that is satisfying right and we have  this calculator online that calculates  live how much we're saving and what what  kind of impacts it has on embedded water  and greenhouse gas emission and so i  feel that i'm actually doing my part and  so yeah i'm very very satisfied  [Music]  [Laughter]

